# RETIRED INPUT - 2026-09-19. The gate that read this file, V17_carve_phase, was
# retired under D9 of 2026-09-19-deliver-nina-cloud-persona. Conservation was a
# ONE-TIME MIGRATION PROOF and it was proven: the gate passed at 71024d1, the commit
# that merged the carve. It is not re-provable once the carved files legitimately
# change, because every table row a later campaign adds lands INSIDE a mapped range
# and fails `C3c within-range`, which has no declaration mechanism by design.
#
# This file is RETAINED, not orphaned: it is the evidence the retirement rests on.
# Do not delete it. See scripts/mozart-contract-gates.sh's V17 header for the full
# disposition, and note that tests/carve/carve-map.tsv is still read by the STANDING
# V23_absence gate.#
# additions.allow - every POST line with no PRE origin, declared and typed (C5, F3/F8).
#
# Types:
#   pointer   a D2 call-site pointer. Asserted MECHANICALLY against the form
#             `**<Trigger>** - read `<FILE>.md` (*<Original section heading>*)`,
#             not merely listed. Each is also asserted to occur EXACTLY once in
#             POST - that is where the duplication guarantee for declared lines
#             lives, since C2 is scoped to PRE lines and cannot see them (F32).
#   stanza    a split's new carved-body heading, or the intake skeleton's heading.
#   ~ changed a REWORDED line, written as a PAIRED block:
#                 ~ changed
#                 - <the PRE line, verbatim>
#                 + <the POST line that replaces it>
#             Subtracted from BOTH channels: from C1 (so a replaced line is not
#             "lost") and from C5 (so its replacement is not "fabricated"). A `-`
#             without its `+`, or a `+` without its `-`, FAILS.
#
# Format for pointer/stanza: <type> TAB <the exact line>
#
# NO PHASE IN THIS CAMPAIGN EXERCISES A `changed` PAIR (D7). A non-zero `~ changed`
# count here is a STOP that returns to the user.
#
# agents/INDEX.md is NOT declared here: it is excluded from conservation (F7/F33),
# is 100% new text, and is gated separately. Declaring it would put several hundred
# lines in this file and bury the pointer lines that actually need review.
#
# PLACEMENT RULE, load-bearing: a declared addition goes BETWEEN mapped ranges,
# never inside one. C3 asserts each range appears as a CONTIGUOUS block in its
# destination, so a pointer inserted mid-range splits the block and fails. Every
# pointer below sits in the gap its own carved section left, which is a range
# boundary by construction.
#
# --- phase 2 -----------------------------------------------------------------
pointer	**Before dispatching any subagent in a repo whose CLAUDE.md is large** — read `CONTEXT-BUDGET.md` (*Subagent context budget (large-CLAUDE.md repos)*) before you brief them.
pointer	**When the work shape is AUDIT** — read `AUDIT.md` (*AUDIT pipeline*) before stage 1.
pointer	**When the work shape is DIAGNOSE** — read `DIAGNOSE.md` (*DIAGNOSE pipeline*) before stage 1.
pointer	**When the work shape is EVAL** — read `EVAL.md` (*EVAL pipeline (mozart evaluating mozart)*) before stage 1.
#
# --- phase 3 -----------------------------------------------------------------
pointer	**When the work shape is OPERATE** — read `OPERATE.md` (*OPERATE pipeline*) before stage 1.
pointer	**When the work shape is INCIDENT** — read `INCIDENT.md` (*INCIDENT pipeline*) before you do anything else.
#
# --- phase 4 -----------------------------------------------------------------
pointer	**Before you create or update any state file** — read `STATE.md` (*State persistence (crash-resume)*).
pointer	**Before narrating a stage transition or drawing the flow** — read `STATE.md` (*Pipeline flow sketch*).
#
# --- phase 5.1 (INTAKE) ------------------------------------------------------
# The boot read is Pattern 1's NAMED MEMBER: unconditional, fires at stage 1 on every
# run and every shape. It uses the ROUTED pointer shape (router first, destination
# second) - see the form note in check-carve-conservation.py.
pointer	**Before step 2 of intake** — read `INDEX.md`, then the file(s) it names for this shape. For every shape that means `INTAKE.md` (*1. Intake*).
pointer	**Before applying a shape boundary test** — read `INTAKE.md` (*Six shapes of work: boundaries and transitions*).
pointer	**Before routing a passthrough** — read `INTAKE.md` (*Single-agent passthrough: routing and discipline*).
# D17 stanzas - these two headings are PINNED by 1c's pointers at PRE :1191 and :1194,
# which are in the conservation baseline and cannot be corrected later.
stanza	## Six shapes of work: boundaries and transitions
stanza	## Single-agent passthrough: routing and discipline
stanza	## Intake (skeleton; the full checklist is in INTAKE.md)
#
# --- phase 5.2 (COUNTERPOINT) ------------------------------------------------
pointer	**Before any sebastian/codex dispatch at stage 5 or 9** — read `COUNTERPOINT.md` (*External tool execution (don't block forever)*).
#
# --- phase 5.3 (FLOWS) -------------------------------------------------------
# The two SPLIT bodies get new declared headings (F12). Neither is cited by a 1c
# pointer, so unlike D17's pair these are not baseline-constrained.
stanza	## Continuing a spawned agent: carve-outs, resume caveat, and narration
stanza	## Build-time flags: the TDD pipeline and auto-detection
pointer	**Before re-spawning an agent you already dispatched this run** — read `FLOWS.md` (*Continuing a spawned agent: carve-outs, resume caveat, and narration*).
pointer	**Before setting a build-time flag** — read `FLOWS.md` (*Build-time flags: the TDD pipeline and auto-detection*).
pointer	**When a run stops early or resumes mid-pipeline** — read `FLOWS.md` (*Partial flows (stop points)*).
pointer	**Before entering the pipeline at a stage other than 1** — read `FLOWS.md` (*Resume / entry points*).
pointer	**Before deciding the slug or searching for prior art** — read `FLOWS.md` (*Run identification and prior-art discovery*).
#
# --- phase 5.4 (WORKTREES) ---------------------------------------------------
pointer	**Before cutting a campaign worktree** — read `WORKTREES.md` (*Worktree isolation (default for code-changing campaigns)*).
pointer	**Before running more than one campaign at a time** — read `WORKTREES.md` (*Multi-campaign mode (parallel orchestration)*).
#
# --- phase 5.5 (TICKETS) -----------------------------------------------------
pointer	**Before resolving a ticketing project, creating a ticket, or posting a phase comment** — read `TICKETS.md` (*Ticket lifecycle*).
#
# --- phase 5.6 (DELIVER) -----------------------------------------------------
pointer	**When you reach DELIVER stage 2 (research) or any later stage** — read `DELIVER.md` (*DELIVER pipeline*) before dispatching anyone.
